---
description: Unit testing conventions for Linkagram business logic
globs: **/src/test/**/*.kt
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing

- Business logic must be testable on the JVM; no emulator, no Robolectric.
- Keep Android UI types out of `core/`, `data/`, and `domain/` so they stay
  testable.
- Network tests use `MockWebServer`. Never call real hosts or real shorteners.
- Inject collaborators through constructor defaults; substitute fakes in tests
  instead of introducing a DI framework or mocking library.
- ViewModel tests inject a `StandardTestDispatcher` and use `runTest`.
- Name tests `subject_condition_expectedResult`.
- Cover at minimum: URL normalization, redirect limit, redirect loops,
  unsupported schemes, malformed `Location` headers, cancellation, provider
  detection, coordinate extraction, invalid coordinates, `lat, lon` formatting.
- Assert on sealed result types rather than on nullable fields.

# Screenshot tests

- Compose preview screenshots live in `app/src/screenshotTest/`, annotated with
  `@PreviewTest` and `@Preview`.
- Reference images live under `app/src/screenshotTestDebug/reference/` and are
  committed.
- Validate with `./gradlew validateDebugScreenshotTest`.
- Run `./gradlew updateDebugScreenshotTest` only after intentional UI changes.
  Never rewrite baselines only to silence a failing build.
- Do not introduce Robolectric for screenshot testing unless ADR-005 is
  superseded.
